From: rgslide-linux <mainline@rgslide>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sdhci-sprd: allow sdio_wifi host on Anbernic RG Slide

Unlike the ZTE MU300 (which uses PCIe Wi-Fi), the Anbernic RG Slide connects
its Marlin3 Wi-Fi/BT combo chip to the SDIO host labeled sprd,name = "sdio_wifi"
(22220000.sdio). Allow "sdio_wifi" through the MU300 probe filter so wcn_bsp
can bind to the SDIO host.

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-sprd.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/sdhci-sprd.c
@@ -803,7 +803,8 @@ static int sdhci_sprd_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	int ret = 0;
 	/* MU300: only the eMMC and the card slot */
 	if (!of_property_read_bool(pdev->dev.of_node, "non-removable") &&
-	    of_property_match_string(pdev->dev.of_node, "sprd,name", "sdio_sd") < 0)
+	    of_property_match_string(pdev->dev.of_node, "sprd,name", "sdio_sd") < 0 &&
+	    of_property_match_string(pdev->dev.of_node, "sprd,name", "sdio_wifi") < 0)
 		return -ENODEV;
 	/* MU300: the card slot waits for the eMMC's host. If that never binds, the card slot stays deferred:
 	 * no SD root without a working eMMC host. */
